  "Convert rights declarations into a workable licensing market instead of a binary open/closed web.": "Bongola ba-esakoli ya makoki na zando ya lisansi oyo esalaka, na esika ya web ya \"efungwami/ekangami\" kaka.",
  "Copied ✓": "Ekopami ✓",
  "Copy": "Kopi",
  "Correct positioning: independent research drafts, protocol proposals, and an open specification experiment.": "Bozwi esika ya solo: mikanda ya bolukiluki ya bonsomi, makanisi ya ba-protokolo, mpe momekano ya spesifikasyo oyo efungwami.",
  "Corrected an earlier default: Belgium (BE) now maps to Dutch instead of French — Flemish speakers are the country’s majority (~60%) over Walloon French speakers (~40%).": "Ebongisami libunga ya kala: Belgique (BE) sikoyo ekei na Néerlandais na esika ya Français — baye balobaka Flamand bazali bato mingi ya mboka (~60%) koleka baye balobaka Français ya Wallonie (~40%).",
  "Corrected an earlier default: Kazakhstan (KZ) now maps to Kazakh instead of Russian, now that a Kazakh translation exists — the same kind of fix as the earlier Belgium correction.": "Ebongisami libunga ya kala: Kazakhstan (KZ) sikoyo ekei na Kazakh na esika ya Russe, sikoyo ete traduction ya Kazakh ezali — ndenge kaka moko ya libongisi ya kala ya Belgique.",
  "Could AI Be Conscious?": "Could AI Be Conscious?",
  "Crawler access rules": "Mibeko ya nzela ya crawler",
  "Crawler simulator": "Simulateur ya crawler",
  "Currency": "Mbongo",
  "Custom tier": "Niveau oyo omisali yo moko",
  "Daily Nous reports on a retracted Journal of Medical Ethics submission containing multiple fabricated, AI-hallucinated references — complete with fake university affiliations and defunct email addresses — that the author reportedly left uncorrected even after being given a chance to fix proofs. The piece contrasts this with Bioethics, whose automated reference-checking would have caught the problem, and argues the real bottleneck isn't detection technology (one commenter's script flagged the fake citations in under a minute) but unpaid reviewer labor and publishing incentives that reward throughput over scrutiny.": "Daily Nous elobi na tina ya mokanda moko oyo elongolamaki na Journal of Medical Ethics, oyo ezalaki na ba-référence mingi ya lokuta oyo AI ekelaki — elongo na ba-université ya lokuta mpe ba-adresse email oyo esali lisusu te — oyo mokomi, bakomelaki, atikaki kobongisa yango ata na nsima ya libaku ya kobongisa bakomi. Lisolo ekokanisi yango na Bioethics, oyo kotala ba-référence na masini elingaki komona likambo yango, mpe elobi ete mokakatano ya solo ezali te tekiniki ya komona (script ya moto moko emonisaki ba-citation ya lokuta na se ya miniti moko), kasi mosala ya ba-relecteur oyo bafutamaka te mpe misala ya ba-éditeur oyo epesaka lifuti na mbangu na esika ya bozindo.",
  "Data free-riding vs. trillion-dollar AI valuations": "Kosalela ba-donnée ofele na esika ya motuya ya AI oyo ekomi na ba-trillion",
  "DeepMind CEO calls for an independent standards body to regulate frontier AI": "DeepMind CEO calls for an independent standards body to regulate frontier AI",
  "Demis Hassabis proposed a FINRA-style regulator for frontier model releases: labs would submit models for review up to 30 days before deployment, voluntary at first, with a path toward mandatory compliance in the US market.": "Demis Hassabis apesaki likanisi ya organisme ya botali oyo ekokani na FINRA mpo na kobima ya ba-modèle ya liboso: ba-laboratoire bakotindaka ba-modèle mpo na kotalama tii na mikolo 30 liboso ya kobima, na ebandeli na bonsomi, na nzela oyo ekei na botosi oyo esengelami na zando ya États-Unis.",
  "Denied": "Eboyami",
  "Deployable policy starter template": "Modèle ya ebandeli ya politiki oyo bakoki kotia",
  "Deployable policy starter template at /downloads/agiright-policy-starter.zip — a minimal static site with the full machine-readable layer, ready for Cloudflare Pages or any static host.": "Modèle ya ebandeli ya politiki oyo bakoki kotia, na /downloads/agiright-policy-starter.zip — site static ya moke oyo ezali na niveau mobimba oyo masini ekoki kotánga, oyo ebongi mpo na Cloudflare Pages to host static nyonso.",
  "Deploying machine-readable policies on your site": "Kotia ba-politiki oyo masini ekoki kotánga na site na yo",
  "Disclaimer": "Likebisi",
  "Distinct from human UI, SEO, or plain APIs, the AI Ingestion & Capability Layer gives websites a machine-facing architecture: a Manifest Layer (entry points like /llms.txt and /ai/manifest.json), a Corpus Layer (machine-readable knowledge), a Capability Layer (agent-callable tools), and a Governance Layer (provenance, licensing, versioning). Static-first, upgradeable toward APIs and MCP. Note: in this paper AICL names the ingestion architecture; on this site's protocol pages AICL refers to the AI Content Licensing Layer.": "Ekeseni na UI ya bato, SEO, to ba-API ya pamba, AI Ingestion & Capability Layer epesaka na ba-site architecture oyo etali masini: Niveau ya Manifest (esika ya kokota lokola /llms.txt na /ai/manifest.json), Niveau ya Corpus (boyebi oyo masini ekoki kotánga), Niveau ya Capacité (bisaleli oyo ajan akoki kobenga), mpe Niveau ya Bokambami (esika eloko ewuti, lisansi, version). Etyami liboso mpo na static, ekoki komata tii na ba-API na MCP. Likebisi: na mokanda oyo, AICL elakisi architecture ya ingestion; na bankasa ya protokolo ya site oyo, AICL elakisi Niveau ya Lisansi ya Contenu ya AI.",
  "Do Large Language Models Possess a Theory of Mind? A Comparative Evaluation Using the Strange Stories Paradigm": "Do Large Language Models Possess a Theory of Mind? A Comparative Evaluation Using the Strange Stories Paradigm",
  "Docs": "Mikanda",
  "Docs / Examples": "Mikanda / Bandakisa",
  "Document library": "Bibliothèque ya mikanda",
  "Does AI have rights — and which framings are even coherent?": "AI ezali na makoki — mpe ba-ndenge nini ya kokanisa yango ezali kutu na ntina?",
  "Download": "Kokitisa",
  "Draft status": "Status ya ebandeli",
  "EU AI Act: What Actually Applies on 2 August 2026": "EU AI Act: What Actually Applies on 2 August 2026",
  "Educational demo: HMAC-SHA256 with a shared secret, showing request-bound, expiring, verifiable license tokens. Production tokens should be signed asymmetrically, with the publisher’s public key discoverable under /.well-known/.": "Démo ya boyekoli: HMAC-SHA256 na sekele oyo esanganami, elakisi ba-jeton ya lisansi oyo ekangani na demande, ezali na ntango ya kosuka, mpe ekoki kotalama. Ba-jeton ya production esengeli kosignama na lolenge ya asymétrique, na fungula ya bato nyonso ya mobimisi oyo ekoki komonana na se ya /.well-known/.",
  "Eight more /topics entries, this time researched by an AI agent rather than curated by hand — same rule as before: every source fetched and confirmed live, summaries an original paraphrase, before anything gets added. 14 entries total.": "Makomi mosusu mwambe ya /topics, mbala oyo elukamaki na ajan ya AI na esika ya kopona na maboko — mobeko kaka moko lokola liboso: liziba nyonso ezwami mpe endimami ete ezali sikoyo, ba-rezime ezali maloba na biso moko, liboso ya kobakisa eloko. Makomi nyonso 14.",
  "Email": "Email",
